# Nib, at Cray & Co.
dialogue nib
  node root nib "Cray and Company. Closed. I'm only here because nobody told me to go home."
    > "What's in all those books?" if not seen:nib.books -> books
    > "I'd like your insurance claims book." if not has claims_book -> claims
    > "How long have you worked here?" if not seen:nib.long -> long
    > "Go home, Nib." if not seen:nib.home -> home
    > "Goodnight." -> bye
  node books nib "No idea. I don't read them. Nobody reads them. That's what they're for."
  node claims nib "I can't give you things. I can only give things to requisitions."
    -> claims2
  node claims2 nib "Requisitions are in the tray. They have to be stamped. I don't read them. I look for the stamp."
  node long nib "Three years. I started the week the Arcadia went. Mr Cray said he needed somebody who never reads anything. I'm the best he's ever had."
  node home nib "Is that an instruction?"
    > "It's a kindness." -> kind
    > "I used to be a clerk. I read everything." -> everything
  node kind nib "We don't have those here. …Could you put it on a form?"
  node everything nib "(horrified) Everything? Even the backs?"
  node bye nib "Is it? I hadn't looked."
  # The stamped requisition (rooms_act4.ts).
  node handed narrator "Nib looks at the stamp, not the words. He takes a fat ledger from pigeonhole one, dusts it with his sleeve, and hands it over without opening it."
    -> nice
  node nice nib "Stamped. Have a nice night."
    > "Do you know what you've just given me?" -> know
    > "Thank you, Nib." -> END
  node know nib "A book."
    -> ruin
  node ruin fenn "Your employer's ruin, more or less."
    > "…" -> stamped
  node stamped nib "Was it stamped? Then it's not my problem. It's the stamp's."
  node after nib "Got another requisition? I like them. They tell you what to do, and then you've done it."
